{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2744","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2744","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2744\",\"parent_revision\":\"ddde6036c5fa848410804f28649e97bd50dd1bcbf8faf8dc4e5b4d2d502ab0ab\",\"root_revision\":\"ddde6036c5fa848410804f28649e97bd50dd1bcbf8faf8dc4e5b4d2d502ab0ab\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nCURRENT STATE: `sam_plan(action='create')`'s `issue` parameter is typed `int | None` and documented as \\\"Optional GitHub issue number\\\" (plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/action_models.py, `CreatePlanConfig.issue`, lines 201-207). This ties the plan-creation issue-linking parameter to GitHub-issue-number semantics specifically.\\n\\nObserved asymmetry: the parallel parameter on the artifact layer, `artifact_register`'s `item_id`, is typed `int | string` and documented as accepting \\\"GitHub issue number (int) or beads nanoid string (e.g. 'bd-a3f8')\\\" \u2014 already generalized across backlog backends. `sam_plan`'s `issue` field was not updated to match when that generalization happened elsewhere.\\n\\nObserved architectural context (plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md, \\\"GistTaskLayer \u2014 Write-Through Plan Storage\\\" and \\\"Backend Providers\\\" sections): the default SAM task backend (`local`, wrapped by `GistTaskLayer`) writes plans through to a GitHub Gist linked from the issue body \u2014 `create_plan` with `issue` set uploads via `artifact_client.store(issue, yaml)`, which requires an actual GitHub issue number. A separate `beads` SAM task backend also exists (`sam_schema/core/backends/beads.py`), documented as mapping \\\"plans to beads epics, tasks to child issues with `--parent` links, context persisted via `bd remember`\\\" \u2014 a different mechanism entirely.\\n\\nWhether beads-backend plan creation reuses the same `issue: int` field, has its own identifier field, or is currently unreachable through `sam_plan(action='create')`'s public MCP interface was not verified in this session.\\n\\nIMPACT: When a non-GitHub backlog backend is configured (e.g. `BACKLOG_BACKEND=beads`), it is unclear from the current schema and documentation whether or how `sam_plan(action='create')` links a plan to that backend's item identifier. This is at minimum a documentation-clarity gap (the parameter name and description are GitHub-specific even though a beads task backend exists), and possibly a functional gap for beads-backend plan-to-item linking depending on what `beads.py`'s `create_plan` implementation actually requires.\\n\\nMEASURABLE SIGNAL: A follow-up investigation determines (1) whether `sam_schema/core/backends/beads.py`'s `create_plan` uses the same `issue: int` MCP parameter or a different path, and (2) whether the parameter should be renamed/retyped to `item_id: int | str` (matching `artifact_register`) or left as-is with corrected documentation, based on what each backend's `create_plan` implementation actually consumes.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **generalize sam_plan create's `issue` field for non-github backlog backends** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 grooming/planning #2722\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-07-10\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-07-10)\\n\\n### Investigation Findings\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-07-10T08:30:54.641755Z</sub>\\n\\nInvestigated 2026-07-10 (same session as filing). Verdict: **not an issue \u2014 closing wontfix.**\\n\\n**Claim 1 checked: is artifact registration broken on a beads-only backend?**\\nNo. `BeadsArtifactProvider` (`plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/beads_artifact_provider.py`) is a complete, tested implementation of the `ArtifactBackend` protocol. `create_artifact_provider('beads')` returns it, and it is selected automatically via the `BACKLOG_BACKEND=beads` env var.\\n- SOURCE: `plugins/development-harness/tests_backlog/test_beads_artifact_provider.py::test_backlog_backend_beads_env_var_selects_provider` (accessed 2026-07-10)\\n- SOURCE: `plugins/development-harness/tests_backlog/test_beads_artifact_provider.py::test_create_artifact_provider_beads_returns_beads_artifact_provider` (accessed 2026-07-10)\\n\\nThe error observed earlier in this session (\\\"`GitHubGistArtifactProvider requires an integer item ID, got '2722'. Use BeadsArtifactProvider for string (beads) item identifiers.`\\\") was misread as evidence of breakage. It is not \u2014 it is `GitHubGistArtifactProvider` (the active provider in this GitHub-backend session) correctly rejecting a string ID and naming the correct provider for beads use. This is the type-enforcement behavior working as intended, not a failure.\\n\\n**Claim 2 checked: does `sam_plan(action='create')`'s `issue: int` field block beads plan-to-item linking?**\\nNo. Read `BeadsTaskProvider.create_plan` directly (`plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/beads.py:525-547`). Its own docstring states: `issue: Optional GitHub issue number stored in plan metadata only.` The actual beads plan-to-item link is established independently inside `create_plan` via a `bd remember` index (`dh.plan-index.{plan_id} \u2192 beads epic ID`), not through the `issue` parameter. A beads-only setup is unaffected by `issue` being int-typed \u2014 the field is optional and unused for the beads linking mechanism.\\n- SOURCE: `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/beads.py` lines 525-547 (accessed 2026-07-10)\\n\\n**Conclusion:** Both artifact assignment and plan-to-item linking work correctly on a pure-beads backend, verified against the actual implementation and its test suite. The originally observed asymmetry (`sam_plan`'s `issue: int | None` vs `artifact_register`'s `item_id: int | str`) is real but does not cause the functional gap this item hypothesized \u2014 `issue` is a vestigial/optional cross-reference field on every backend's `create_plan`, not the mechanism that establishes item linkage. No functional fix is needed. Retyping `issue` to `int | str` would not enable any currently-blocked capability.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"74324c36270c3e96f9f2586b86e29a7bae5a05162d2e3ea70975a3e00df81d1e\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCJSxg\"}"}